igned vertical bars into horizontal bars resting on the same baseline.\nInput structure\n- The grid has a background and bottom-aligned, one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Blue bars are markers; red bars are body bars that may be chained after a marker.\nRule\n- Starting at each blue bar, repeatedly include the next red bar whose column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height.\n- Clear every included vertical bar, then redraw each included bar horizontally to the right from its original bottom cell, with length equal to its vertical height.\n- Red bars that are not reached from a blue marker remain unchanged.\nKey insight\n- A vertical bar's height is also the width it occupies after rotation, so the chain follows immediate horizontal contact after each rotated bar.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars on the background; blue bars start chains and red bars may follow\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each blue-started chain, rotate each reached vertical bar clockwise onto the shared baseline; the next red bar is reached when its column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3522\nmechanism=0.4112\nlexical=0.0201\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d93c6891\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3188\nmechanism=0.3764\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:line_segment, operation:count, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d93c6891.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d93c6891.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove each gray bar into its adjacent orange rectangle as full stripes from the contacted edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The scene uses black outside space, yellow fill, gray one-cell-thick bars, and solid orange rectangles.\n- Each gray bar 4-touches exactly one orange rectangle; some orange rectangles have no touching gray bar.\n- Gray bars touching the same orange rectangle all have the same orientation.\n\nRule\n- Recolor every original gray cell to yellow.\n- For each orange rectangle touched by gray bars, count the gray cells assigned to that rectangle.\n- Horizontal gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange rows starting from the contacted top or bottom row.\n- Vertical gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange columns starting from the contacted left or right column.\n- Orange rectangles with no touching gray bar remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The gray pixels are not copied by shape; their count is transferred into the neighboring orange rectangle as edge-aligned row or column stripes.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"gray one-cell-thick bars s\",\n  \"dst\": \"4-adjacent solid orange rectangles d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s 4-touches d\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase s to yellow; in each matched d, repaint |matched s cells| orange cells gray as complete rows for horizontal bars or complete columns for vertical bars from the touched edge\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aa62e3f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3111\nmechanism=0.3353\nlexical=0.0154\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:marker, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/aa62e3f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace the outlined object with the outside contour of that outline in the marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n- The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n- One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n  is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\nRule:\n- Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n- Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n  marker color.\n- Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\nlargest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one 8-connected largest foreground outline object and smaller interior marker colors on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase all original foreground pixels; repaint the background pixels 4-adjacent to the outline with the unique smallest non-outline marker color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"963c33f8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3167\nmechanism=0.4023\nlexical=0.0157\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:line_segment, object:marker, operation:count, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/963c33f8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the columns of the top marker downward, stopping blue-ended columns on grey obstacles and letting maroon-ended columns pass to the bottom.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The most numerous non-background color forms stationary grey obstacle pixels.\n- The other two colors form a single 3x3 top-edge marker whose top two rows\n  are maroon and whose bottom row contains maroon or blue control pixels.\n\nRule\n- Erase the top marker.\n- Treat each marker column as a vertical drop retaining its three colors.\n- A column whose bottom control pixel is blue stops immediately above the\n  first grey pixel below that column, or bottom-aligns if none exists.\n- Contiguous maroon-ended columns pass through obstacles and bottom-align;\n  if such a run has a clear down-right slide from a grey ledge, shift the\n  run one column right before bottom-aligning.\n- When a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear\n  the rest of the marker-width gap in that bottom bar.\n\nKey insight\n- The bottom row of the top marker is a control strip: blue cells mean\n  \"stick to the first obstacle,\" while maroon cells mean \"fall through.\"\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"columns of the 3x3 maroon/blue marker on the top edge; the bottom cell of each column is the control pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop in each marker column; blue-ended columns stop above the first grey obstacle below, while maroon-ended runs pass through to the bottom with a one-column right slide from a clear grey ledge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"copy each three-pixel marker column intact; contiguous maroon-ended columns are tested as one run for the slide\",\n  \"dst\": \"settled positions on the same canvas after erasing the top marker\",\n  \"transform\": \"if a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear the rest of the marker-width gap in that bar; leave other grey obstacles fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3039\nmechanism=0.3252\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's un